  "multipliers": {"gdpGrowth": 0.85, "militarySpending": 1.2, "stability": 0.95},
  "briefing": [
    "Ukraine: Russia holds about a fifth of the country but has gained almost nothing in 2026; a local Oleshky ceasefire and US-brokered Abu Dhabi talks are the only diplomacy in play.",
    "Iran: since the February strikes killed Ali Khamenei, an undeclared war and a US naval blockade grind on; Mojtaba Khamenei is Supreme Leader but is reportedly wounded and rarely seen.",
    "Over 200 kg of 60% enriched uranium is believed to sit intact in Isfahan's tunnels; inspectors have had no access since February.",
    "Red Sea: the Houthis took Mokha in September and reportedly Perim; a Saudi-backed counteroffensive began in October after a strike on Riyadh's airport.",
    "New START expired in February: for the first time since 1972 no treaty limits US and Russian strategic forces.",
    "Taiwan Strait: Beijing rehearsed a blockade of Keelung and Kaohsiung last December, while Taipei's opposition halved Lai's special defence budget.",
    "Trade: the Supreme Court struck down Trump's emergency tariffs in February; a 10% global tariff replaced them, and allies from Ottawa to Copenhagen are still smarting.",
    "This week: US midterms (3 Nov), Israel's hung-Knesset count (4 Nov), and Brazil's losing camp contesting Lula's narrow re-election."
  ],
